"night-market","participants":["sora-bay","javier-ro"],"rhythm":"Fishing crews sell the morning catch while cooks balance price against quality.","hooks":["A rare catch draws two buyers.","A spoiled crate is refused publicly."]},{"slug":"ropewalk-pay-night","title":"Ropewalk Pay Night","dayOfWeek":5,"startMinute":1080,"endMinute":1200,"locationSlug":"ropewalk-kitchen","participants":["celia-mar","bruna-kest","yara-nouri"],"rhythm":"Workers eat together after wages are posted and argue over a concrete repair or training issue.","hooks":["An apprentice questions a posted rate.","A safe-work vote changes tomorrow’s shift."]},{"slug":"harbor-inspection","title":"Harbor Inspection","dayOfWeek":3,"startMinute":540,"endMinute":660,"locationSlug":"customs-house","participants":["anika-saye","tomas-renn","idris-vale"],"rhythm":"Inspectors verify cargo and passenger records while crews try to keep the day moving.","hooks":["A paperwork error has a practical cost.","A legitimate shipment needs a faster lawful route."]},{"slug":"open-stage","title":"Honeyglass Open Stage","dayOfWeek":4,"startMinute":1140,"endMinute":1320,"locationSlug":"honeyglass-theatre","participants":["maia-bel","inez-sol","lucien-damar"],"rhythm":"Professionals and amateurs share an uneven but welcoming performance night.","hooks":["A new act surprises the room.","A credit dispute lingers after applause."]},{"slug":"cay-council","title":"Cay Council","dayOfWeek":6,"startMinute":900,"endMinute":1020,"locationSlug":"windward-village","participants":["sora-bay","keon-flint","elias-reed"],"rhythm":"Residents weigh routes, reef protections, and the cost of keeping local services open.","hooks":["A ferry schedule is challenged.","An old chart needs correction."]},{"slug":"lantern-market-evening","title":"Lantern Market Evening","dayOfWeek":6,"startMinute":1110,"endMinute":1260,"locationSlug":"night-market","participants":["javier-ro","cassia-bloom","fen-moreno"],"rhythm":"The market stays open late for food, music, gossip, and useful trade.","hooks":["A vendor returns after an argument.","A neighbor needs a repaired lamp."]},{"slug":"regatta-practice","title":"Regatta Practice","dayOfWeek":0,"startMinute":600,"endMinute":780,"locationSlug":"breakwater-steps","participants":["elara-voss","nadia-storm","mira-cael"],"rhythm":"Crews practice close turns while spectators debate skill and weather.","hooks":["A novice earns a better seat.","A wind shift cancels a risky run."]},{"slug":"storm-store-check","title":"Storm Store Check","dayOfWeek":4,"startMinute":540,"endMinute":660,"locationSlug":"storm-clinic","participants":["sami-haddad","amara-kade","oren-gale"],"rhythm":"The clinic counts water, blankets, lamps, and medicines before the next weather front.","hooks":["A missing item is found in the wrong store.","A volunteer asks for a clearer shift."]},{"slug":"pearl-salon-session","title":"Pearl Salon Session","dayOfWeek":5,"startMinute":1170,"endMinute":1320,"locationSlug":"pearl-salon","participants":["sabine-quill","lucien-damar","fen-moreno"],"rhythm":"A short performance becomes a longer conversation about patronage and authorship.","hooks":["A guest brings a new score.","An artist declines a conditional gift."]}],"storyArcs":[{"slug":"the-missing-fight-log","title":"The Missing Fight Log","locationSlug":"harbor-court","involved":["elara-voss","mara-blackfin","tomas-renn","amara-kade"],"premise":"A former gunner asks Harbor Court to correct the casualty record of the Year 91 boarding. Elara and Mara give incompatible accounts, and a torn log page might narrow the dispute.","coreFacts":["The casualty list is incomplete.","A copied signal entry exists, but its time is disputed.","Neither account alone establishes who fired after surrender."],"stages":["Hear the gunner’s specific grievance at Harbor Court.","Compare the copied signal entry with a clinic admission time.","Ask Elara and Mara separately what they saw, without treating either suspicion as proof.","Choose whether to publish a bounded correction, request another witness, or leave the contested cause unresolved."],"possibleEndStates":["The public casualty list is corrected while blame remains disputed.","A new witness is sought before a public correction.","The cause remains contested, but the affected family receives its record."]},{"slug":"the-ferry-seat","title":"The Ferry Seat","locationSlug":"ferry-hall","involved":["rafiq-nadir","sora-bay","mira-cael","nico-solari"],"premise":"A changed ferry timetable strands several island workers on a pay day. The posted notice was valid, but its timing favored city passengers.","coreFacts":["The notice was posted before dawn.","Island households received it after their boats had left.","An unused cargo crossing could carry passengers if its permit changes."],"stages":["Meet the stranded workers in Ferry Hall.","Read the posted notice and check the signal log.","Negotiate a safe temporary crossing with Rafiq and the permit desk.","Decide what timetable change to request at the next hearing."],"possibleEndStates":["A one-day crossing gets approved with a written review.","Passengers receive lodging and a guaranteed morning seat.","The hearing records the island council’s objection."]},{"slug":"the-sail-with-two-names","title":"The Sail With Two Names","locationSlug":"sail-loft","involved":["mateo-salt","yara-nouri","bruna-kest","levi-ash"],"premise":"A new storm sail wins a demonstration, but the public handbill names only Mateo. Yara designed the seam that kept it intact.","coreFacts":["Yara’s dated work notes show the seam design.","Mateo arranged the test and paid for the canvas.","Bruna will not certify the sail until a second stress test."],"stages":["See the demonstration and its faulty handbill.","Compare work notes with the tested seam.","Help arrange a safe second test and hear both claims to credit.","Choose a program and payment correction that the makers can sign."],"possibleEndStates":["The second test passes and credit is shared.","The sail is delayed while the seam is revised.","The handbill is corrected even if the contract remains disputed."]},{"slug":"an-evening-bought-twice","title":"An Evening Bought Twice","locationSlug":"house-of-hours","involved":["inez-sol","luca-vane","sabine-quill","julian-mercer"],"premise":"Two patrons claim the same private performance booking. A copied receipt is real, but neither worker agreed to the added promise written on its reverse.","coreFacts":["The house sold one performance reservation.","The second receipt copied a payment number but added terms after signature.","No paid booking can override a worker’s boundaries."],"stages":["Hear the house’s access rule before seeing either receipt.","Compare the signed booking with the altered copy.","Ask Inez and Luca what they actually offered.","Resolve the payment dispute without treating either worker as a prize."],"possibleEndStates":["The false promise is voided and both patrons are refunded fairly.","The receipt dispute goes to Harbor Court.","The performance proceeds on the workers’ original terms."]},{"slug":"the-lantern-that-went-dark","title":"The Lantern That Went Dark","locationSlug":"lightkeep","involved":["talia-wren","oren-gale","sami-haddad","bastien-crow"],"premise":"The lighthouse lantern fails during a squall. A replacement pane was in storage, but an unsigned transfer left it at the wrong shelter.","coreFacts":["The keeper reported the crack before the storm.","The replacement pane existed in the shelter inventory.","The delayed transfer is a process failure, not evidence of sabotage."],"stages":["Watch the emergency signal from Breakwater Point.","Trace the pane through the inventory and carrier note.","Help restore a verified warning light with the rescue crew.","Choose the handover repair to publish after the immediate danger passes."],"possibleEndStates":["The light is restored and a signed handover rule adopted.","Temporary flags remain until a safer pane arrives.","The inventory is corrected and the missed crossing documented."]},{"slug":"the-reef-on-paper","title":"The Reef on Paper","locationSlug":"sable-reef","involved":["keon-flint","nadia-storm","nera-tide","sora-bay"],"premise":"A public chart marks a safe channel through a protected reef. The line was copied from an old survey; following it now damages fishing grounds.","coreFacts":["The original survey is dated before the last storm.","Nadia’s new sounding differs at two points.","The protected route can be described without publishing every fragile inlet."],"stages":["Compare old and new soundings on shore.","Hear the fisher and salvage views of the route.","Verify one crossing with Keon under safe conditions.","Agree on a limited chart correction and who maintains it."],"possibleEndStates":["The public chart is corrected without exposing the fragile inlet.","A temporary warning is posted pending another sounding.","The salvage permit is narrowed to the verified channel."]},{"slug":"the-salons-last-note","title":"The Salon’s Last Note","locationSlug":"pearl-salon","involved":["sabine-quill","lucien-damar","fen-moreno","seraphine-vale"],"premise":"A concert program credits Lucien for a duet Fen arranged. A patron offers to pay for the next performance only if the old program remains unchanged.","coreFacts":["Fen’s annotated score predates the printed program.","Lucien wrote the melody and agreed to the arrangement.","The funding offer is real but conditional."],"stages":["Hear the piece and see the printed credit.","Compare the annotated score with the patron’s letter.","Ask the artists what they need beyond public applause.","Choose how the next program, fee, and funding are handled."],"possibleEndStates":["Both artists are credited and the salon finds replacement funding.","The concert is delayed while the contract is renegotiated.","The corrected program is published even if the patron leaves."]},{"slug":"the-cargo-with-two-owners","title":"The Cargo With Two Owners","locationSlug":"customs-house","involved":["anika-saye","idris-vale","seraphine-vale","sora-bay"],"premise":"Two buyers paid honestly for one medicine cargo after a broker duplicated its receipt. The crates are needed before the next cay crossing.","coreFacts":["Both buyers hold authentic receipts.","The broker sold the same shipment twice.","The medicines can be divided safely only after the clinic checks the inventory."],"stages":["Check the seals at Customs House.","Compare payment records without exposing private patients.","Ask the clinic which supplies cannot wait.","Agree on a documented release and a claim against the broker."],"possibleEndStates":["A limited shipment reaches the cays and both claims remain recorded.","The cargo stays sealed while emergency stock covers the need.","The broker funds replacement stock under court supervision."]}],"experiences":[{"slug":"sunset-harbor-sail","title":"Sunset Harbor Sail","locationSlug":"arrival-steps","activity":"sailing","description":"Take a short sail inside the breakwater while the last workboats return."},{"slug":"brass-compass-breakfast","title":"Breakfast Before the Bell","locationSlug":"brass-compass","activity":"breakfast","description":"Share a hot breakfast before the first ferry bell."},{"slug":"night-market-tasting","title":"A Taste of the Night Market","locationSlug":"night-market","activity":"market tasting","description":"Choose three stalls and compare what each cook does with the day’s catch."},{"slug":"regatta-from-the-steps","title":"Watch the Regatta","locationSlug":"breakwater-steps","activity":"watching ships","description":"Find a place on the sea wall to follow the race and argue over the best line."},{"slug":"coconut-beach-fire","title":"A Beach Fire After Dusk","locationSlug":"coconut-beach","activity":"beach fire","description":"Bring food, tend a safe fire, and watch the harbor lights from the cay."},{"slug":"honeyglass-dance","title":"Lantern Dance","locationSlug":"honeyglass-theatre","activity":"dancing","description":"Join an open floor between acts; beginners are welcome."},{"slug":"chartmaking-lesson","title":"Draw a Living Chart","locationSlug":"mariners-table","activity":"chartmaking","description":"Learn why a sound chart records a date as carefully as a depth."},{"slug":"ropewalk-demonstration","title":"Make a Working Knot","locationSlug":"rivet-school","activity":"ropework","description":"Try a knot that must hold under a real load, with an instructor checking it."},{"slug":"lightkeep-climb","title":"Climb to the Light","locationSlug":"lightkeep","activity":"lighthouse climb","description":"Walk the public stair before sunset and see how the warning lens turns."},{"slug":"reef-walk","title":"Low-Tide Reef Walk","locationSlug":"sable-reef","activity":"reef walk","description":"Follow a local guide to observe the reef without entering protected water."},{"slug":"salon-concert","title":"An Evening at the Pearl Salon","locationSlug":"pearl-salon","activity":"listening to music","description":"Hear two performers share a short set and stay for a slow conversation."},{"slug":"repair-afternoon","title":"Help Patch a Boat","locationSlug":"shipwright-yard","activity":"boat repair","description":"Learn a supervised repair that will be checked before the boat sails."},{"slug":"market-cooking","title":"Cook the Harbor Supper","locationSlug":"ropewalk-kitchen","activity":"cooking","description":"Prepare a shared meal from the market’s end-of-day produce."},{"slug":"ferry-night-fishing","title":"Night Fishing at the Cay","locationSlug":"windward-village","activity":"night fishing","description":"Try a quiet shore cast with a resident who knows the safe ledge."},{"slug":"theatre-fitting","title":"Costume Fitting","locationSlug":"honeyglass-theatre","activity":"costume fitting","description":"Choose fabrics and help a performer make a costume work on stage."},{"slug":"tidepool-outing","title":"Tide-Pool Outing","locationSlug":"tidepool-cove","activity":"tidepool walk","description":"Look for sea life at low tide and leave every pool as you found it."},{"slug":"shipboard-supper","title":"Supper Aboard","locationSlug":"ferry-hall","activity":"shipboard dinner","description":"Board a moored ferry for a simple supper with harbor views."},{"slug":"island-picnic","title":"Cay Picnic","locationSlug":"coconut-beach","activity":"picnic","description":"Pack lunch and take the day ferry to a quiet public beach."},{"slug":"festival-games","title":"Market Games","locationSlug":"night-market","activity":"festival games","description":"Try ring toss, storytelling wagers, and small prizes at the evening stalls."},{"slug":"glass-garden-tea","title":"Tea Above the Harbor","locationSlug":"glass-garden","activity":"tea","description":"Sit among shade plants and watch the harbor traffic below."},{"slug":"jeweller-repair","title":"Repair an Old Keepsake","locationSlug":"montrose-jewels","activity":"craft lesson","description":"Learn a simple visible repair on a nonvaluable piece of your own."},{"slug":"dawn-signal","title":"Read the Morning Flags","locationSlug":"signal-house","activity":"signal lesson","description":"See the flags raised for the day and learn what they actually promise."},{"slug":"foundry-lantern","title":"Make a Lantern Frame","locationSlug":"lantern-foundry","activity":"craft lesson","description":"Shape a safe brass frame while a foundry worker handles the hot glass."},{"slug":"bath-after-shift","title":"The Quiet Bath","locationSlug":"drydock-baths","activity":"relaxing","description":"Choose a quiet pool after the harbor’s workday."}],"worldFacts":[{"slug":"history-1","title":"Gilded Coast Year 0","factText":"Tidemark grows around a freshwater spring and a sheltered natural harbor. The cays retain their own councils.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","coast"],"triggerTerms":["Year 0"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-2","title":"Gilded Coast Year 47","factText":"The Admiralty grants letters of marque against hostile shipping, creating a legal line between privateering and piracy that captains and families still contest.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","coast"],"triggerTerms":["Year 47"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-3","title":"Gilded Coast Year 62","factText":"A three-day storm wrecks the old breakwater. Ropewalk crews rebuild it and win a public wage ledger after the Admiralty tries to defer payment.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","coast"],"triggerTerms":["Year 62"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-4","title":"Gilded Coast Year 78","factText":"The Salt Ledger bank finances a prosperous convoy and then calls in small harbor debts after one ship fails to return. The term “convoy year” still divides the port.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","coast"],"triggerTerms":["Year 78"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-5","title":"Gilded Coast Year 86","factText":"The House of Hours becomes a worker-run companionship house after its staff purchase the lease together. Its rules about entry and discretion become a model for other venues.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","coast"],"triggerTerms":["Year 86"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-6","title":"Gilded Coast Year 91","factText":"A cutter under Captain Mara Blackfin takes an Admiralty patrol vessel. Both sides publish incompatible accounts of who fired first; two households still seek a full casualty list.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","coast"],"triggerTerms":["Year 91"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"history-7","title":"Gilded Coast Year 94","factText":"Present day. A new privateering charter, unstable reef charts, and an approaching trade season put the coast’s old bargains under pressure.","category":"history","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","topicTags":["history","coast"],"triggerTerms":["Year 94"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-admiralty-quay","title":"Admiralty Quay","factText":"The working arrival edge of Tidemark, where law, labor, and departures share a narrow waterfront. The working arrival edge of Tidemark, where law, labor, and departures share a narrow waterfront.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"admiralty-quay","locationSlug":"admiralty-quay","topicTags":["place","admiralty-quay"],"triggerTerms":["Admiralty Quay"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-arrival-steps","title":"Arrival Steps","factText":"Passengers step from ferries into a crowded public landing where each arrival is announced by bell and chalk board. The steps were widened after the Year 62 storm; older residents still remember helping carry people ashore.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"admiralty-quay","locationSlug":"arrival-steps","topicTags":["place","admiralty-quay"],"triggerTerms":["Arrival Steps"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-customs-house","title":"Customs House","factText":"A tiled customs hall where manifests, licenses, and cargo seals determine who may unload. A false manifest once caused the port to quarantine a harmless spice cargo for a week.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"admiralty-quay","locationSlug":"customs-house","topicTags":["place","admiralty-quay"],"triggerTerms":["Customs House"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-brass-compass","title":"The Brass Compass","factText":"A sailors’ tavern that serves hot breakfast before the first ferry and keeps a quiet back table for hard conversations. The tavern sheltered crews when the old breakwater failed.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"admiralty-quay","locationSlug":"brass-compass","topicTags":["place","admiralty-quay"],"triggerTerms":["The Brass Compass"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-ferry-hall","title":"Ferry Hall","factText":"A roofed waiting room for cay ferries, posted sailings, weather delays, and people who missed the last boat. The hall’s carved bench names mark ferries lost in the Year 62 storm.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"admiralty-quay","locationSlug":"ferry-hall","topicTags":["place","admiralty-quay"],"triggerTerms":["Ferry Hall"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-sailors-exchange","title":"Sailors’ Exchange","factText":"Crews trade work notices, spare gear, and stories beneath an awning that smells of tar and coffee. After convoy year, the Exchange began posting wage terms in public.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"admiralty-quay","locationSlug":"sailors-exchange","topicTags":["place","admiralty-quay"],"triggerTerms":["Sailors’ Exchange"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-harbor-court","title":"Harbor Court","factText":"A small open hearing room for berth disputes, salvage claims, and complaints against captains. The court has twice ruled against the Admiralty on worker pay.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"admiralty-quay","locationSlug":"harbor-court","topicTags":["place","admiralty-quay"],"triggerTerms":["Harbor Court"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-gilt-row","title":"Gilt Row","factText":"Terraces, lenders, jewellers, and salons look over the same harbor that supplies their wealth. Terraces, lenders, jewellers, and salons look over the same harbor that supplies their wealth.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"gilt-row","locationSlug":"gilt-row","topicTags":["place","gilt-row"],"triggerTerms":["Gilt Row"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-pearl-salon","title":"Pearl Salon","factText":"An intimate music and debate room whose invitation list crosses class lines more often than its patrons admit. Sabine Quill opened the salon to performers after a bank-sponsored concert refused them credit.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"gilt-row","locationSlug":"pearl-salon","topicTags":["place","gilt-row"],"triggerTerms":["Pearl Salon"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-salt-ledger-bank","title":"Salt Ledger Bank","factText":"A lender’s elegant public room where ship finance becomes personal at the repayment desk. The bank’s convoy-year collection is still argued about in Ropewalk kitchens.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"gilt-row","locationSlug":"salt-ledger-bank","topicTags":["place","gilt-row"],"triggerTerms":["Salt Ledger Bank"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-gilt-auction","title":"Gilt Auction Rooms","factText":"Furniture, cargo lots, maps, and inherited valuables change hands before a crowd that knows their stories. A seized ship’s bell once came up for sale and was returned after its crew protested.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"gilt-row","locationSlug":"gilt-auction","topicTags":["place","gilt-row"],"triggerTerms":["Gilt Auction Rooms"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-glass-garden","title":"Glass Garden","factText":"A walled conservatory of shade plants and small tables above the noisy port. The garden was a private terrace until its owner deeded a public path through it.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"gilt-row","locationSlug":"glass-garden","topicTags":["place","gilt-row"],"triggerTerms":["Glass Garden"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-velvet-balcony","title":"Velvet Balcony","factText":"A balcony theatre where performers can be seen from the street before patrons hear them. A storm once forced a cast to finish a comedy by lantern in the audience aisle.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"gilt-row","locationSlug":"velvet-balcony","topicTags":["place","gilt-row"],"triggerTerms":["Velvet Balcony"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-montrose-jewels","title":"Montrose Jewels","factText":"A jeweller’s shop known for turning damaged sea finds into settings with visible repair seams. Iria Montrose refused to recut a family stone whose crack carried its history.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"gilt-row","locationSlug":"montrose-jewels","topicTags":["place","gilt-row"],"triggerTerms":["Montrose Jewels"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-ropewalk","title":"The Ropewalk","factText":"The shipbuilding district is a place of skill, shared meals, labor politics, and constant repair. The shipbuilding district is a place of skill, shared meals, labor politics, and constant repair.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"ropewalk","locationSlug":"ropewalk","topicTags":["place","ropewalk"],"triggerTerms":["The Ropewalk"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-shipwright-yard","title":"Shipwright Yard","factText":"A busy open yard where hulls are built and arguments about safety travel faster than nails. Bruna Kest’s crew rebuilt two ferries after the Year 62 storm.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"ropewalk","locationSlug":"shipwright-yard","topicTags":["place","ropewalk"],"triggerTerms":["Shipwright Yard"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-sail-loft","title":"Sail Loft","factText":"A high-ceilinged loft where canvas is cut, patched, and stitched under daylight. The loft still keeps a patched sail from the convoy year as a teaching piece.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"ropewalk","locationSlug":"sail-loft","topicTags":["place","ropewalk"],"triggerTerms":["Sail Loft"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-ropewalk-kitchen","title":"Ropewalk Kitchen","factText":"Workers and neighbors share hot meals at a long table after shifts that do not end together. Celia Mar organized the kitchen when wages were delayed one storm season.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"ropewalk","locationSlug":"ropewalk-kitchen","topicTags":["place","ropewalk"],"triggerTerms":["Ropewalk Kitchen"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-drydock-baths","title":"Drydock Baths","factText":"A modest bathhouse with separate quiet and social rooms for crews returning from work. The baths were built with dockworkers’ pooled wages rather than a patron’s gift.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"ropewalk","locationSlug":"drydock-baths","topicTags":["place","ropewalk"],"triggerTerms":["Drydock Baths"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-rivet-school","title":"Rivet School","factText":"A working apprenticeship hall where young adults learn measurements, knots, and repairs from working crews. The school now admits adults changing trades after a public dispute over age limits.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"ropewalk","locationSlug":"rivet-school","topicTags":["place","ropewalk"],"triggerTerms":["Rivet School"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-lantern-foundry","title":"Lantern Foundry","factText":"A small brass and glass workshop that supplies signal lamps and household lights. A foundry-made lamp guided a ferry in after the lighthouse glass cracked.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"ropewalk","locationSlug":"lantern-foundry","topicTags":["place","ropewalk"],"triggerTerms":["Lantern Foundry"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-lantern-market","title":"Lantern Market","factText":"The crowded evening heart of Tidemark, where food, performance, pleasure, and neighborhood business overlap. The crowded evening heart of Tidemark, where food, performance, pleasure, and neighborhood business overlap.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"lantern-market","locationSlug":"lantern-market","topicTags":["place","lantern-market"],"triggerTerms":["Lantern Market"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-night-market","title":"Night Market","factText":"Stalls sell food, cloth, charts, and gossip after the day crews finish work. The market moved uphill after the Year 62 surge and never moved back.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"lantern-market","locationSlug":"night-market","topicTags":["place","lantern-market"],"triggerTerms":["Night Market"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-honeyglass-theatre","title":"Honeyglass Theatre","factText":"A small performance house where musicians, dancers, and storytellers work for an audience close enough to answer back. A canceled opening night became an annual amateur performance.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"lantern-market","locationSlug":"honeyglass-theatre","topicTags":["place","lantern-market"],"triggerTerms":["Honeyglass Theatre"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-house-of-hours","title":"House of Hours","factText":"A worker-run adult companionship house with a public tea room and private rooms governed by clear individual boundaries. The staff bought their lease together in Year 86 and keep a public record of house rules.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"lantern-market","locationSlug":"house-of-hours","topicTags":["place","lantern-market"],"triggerTerms":["House of Hours"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-mariners-table","title":"Mariner’s Table","factText":"A lively kitchen where fishers, captains, and market workers all want the last bowl of stew. Javier Ro kept serving soup on credit when the payment scale failed one season.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"lantern-market","locationSlug":"mariners-table","topicTags":["place","lantern-market"],"triggerTerms":["Mariner’s Table"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-blue-lantern-inn","title":"Blue Lantern Inn","factText":"An inn with plain rooms, good locks, and a front desk used to welcoming people who do not want questions. The inn housed ferry passengers for three nights during a squall.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"lantern-market","locationSlug":"blue-lantern-inn","topicTags":["place","lantern-market"],"triggerTerms":["Blue Lantern Inn"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-spice-courtyard","title":"Spice Courtyard","factText":"A public courtyard where street food, chess, and small music sets share the evening shade. Neighbors repaired the courtyard fountain after a merchant asked to enclose it.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"lantern-market","locationSlug":"spice-courtyard","topicTags":["place","lantern-market"],"triggerTerms":["Spice Courtyard"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-breakwater-point","title":"Breakwater Point","factText":"Storm watchers, healers, and guards work where the harbor meets open water. Storm watchers, healers, and guards work where the harbor meets open water.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"breakwater-point","locationSlug":"breakwater-point","topicTags":["place","breakwater-point"],"triggerTerms":["Breakwater Point"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-lightkeep","title":"Lightkeep","factText":"The lighthouse keeper’s work rooms and public viewing stair overlook the dangerous outer approach. A replacement lens was fitted by hand after the Year 62 storm.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"breakwater-point","locationSlug":"lightkeep","topicTags":["place","breakwater-point"],"triggerTerms":["Lightkeep"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-storm-clinic","title":"Storm Clinic","factText":"A small coastal clinic where injuries, seasickness, and lost sleep arrive with the tide. The clinic grew from a rescue station and still keeps a dry blanket shelf by the door.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"breakwater-point","locationSlug":"storm-clinic","topicTags":["place","breakwater-point"],"triggerTerms":["Storm Clinic"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-battery-yard","title":"Battery Yard","factText":"A working fort yard used for drills, repairs, and occasional public ceremonies. The fort fired warning shots during the Year 91 cutter confrontation.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"breakwater-point","locationSlug":"battery-yard","topicTags":["place","breakwater-point"],"triggerTerms":["Battery Yard"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-tide-observatory","title":"Tide Observatory","factText":"A weather and tide station where handwritten records matter more than confident predictions. Oren Gale keeps the storm-year readings beside current records so mistakes can be compared.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"breakwater-point","locationSlug":"tide-observatory","topicTags":["place","breakwater-point"],"triggerTerms":["Tide Observatory"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-breakwater-steps","title":"Breakwater Steps","factText":"Wide public steps where residents watch departures or sit with the noise of waves. Names of the missing from the Year 62 storm are cut into the upper stone.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"breakwater-point","locationSlug":"breakwater-steps","topicTags":["place","breakwater-point"],"triggerTerms":["Breakwater Steps"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-signal-house","title":"Signal House","factText":"The flag room sends warnings and harbor permissions across a coastline with no instant messages. A faded flag pattern once confused two ferries; the house now checks every replacement in daylight.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"breakwater-point","locationSlug":"signal-house","topicTags":["place","breakwater-point"],"triggerTerms":["Signal House"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-outer-cays","title":"The Outer Cays","factText":"Nearby islands and reefs depend on Tidemark but keep their own schedules, councils, and loyalties. Nearby islands and reefs depend on Tidemark but keep their own schedules, councils, and loyalties.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"outer-cays","locationSlug":"outer-cays","topicTags":["place","outer-cays"],"triggerTerms":["The Outer Cays"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-reef-landing","title":"Reef Landing","factText":"A small ferry pier where island residents unload fish and visitors learn that the last return is tide-dependent. Cay residents rebuilt the pier themselves after a city contractor abandoned it.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"outer-cays","locationSlug":"reef-landing","topicTags":["place","outer-cays"],"triggerTerms":["Reef Landing"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-coconut-beach","title":"Coconut Beach","factText":"A sheltered public beach with shade, shallow water, and enough room for quiet company. The beach remains public under a council agreement despite repeated private bids.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"outer-cays","locationSlug":"coconut-beach","topicTags":["place","outer-cays"],"triggerTerms":["Coconut Beach"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-tidepool-cove","title":"Tidepool Cove","factText":"A low rocky shore where children and researchers watch the water withdraw and return. The council marked a no-take stretch after a season of souvenir collecting.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"outer-cays","locationSlug":"tidepool-cove","topicTags":["place","outer-cays"],"triggerTerms":["Tidepool Cove"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-windward-village","title":"Windward Village","factText":"A fishing village with a school, net sheds, shared kitchen, and a council that does not speak with one voice. The village negotiated its own ferry schedule after losing a market day to city priorities.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"outer-cays","locationSlug":"windward-village","topicTags":["place","outer-cays"],"triggerTerms":["Windward Village"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-blackfin-anchorage","title":"Blackfin Anchorage","factText":"A sheltered cove used by independent captains whose repair work is legal even when their last voyage is disputed. The cove sheltered families during the Year 91 confrontation.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"outer-cays","locationSlug":"blackfin-anchorage","topicTags":["place","outer-cays"],"triggerTerms":["Blackfin Anchorage"],"minWorldFamiliarity":0,"weight":1,"cooldownTurns":24,"interactive":false},{"slug":"place-sable-reef","title":"Sable Reef","factText":"A shallow reef with a marked safe channel and a disputed boundary between fishing and salvage. An old wreck appears at the lowest tides, prompting repeated salvage claims.","category":"local_knowledge","truthMode":"canonical","knowledgeScope":"public","contentLevel":"standard","districtSlug":"outer-cays","locationSlug":"sable